# Porch Light, by Grok, Claude & SZ. Original slow indie in the Alt rock style:
# clean guitar up front, a piano underneath, a vocal-style hook that
# saves the loud band for the last chorus. Written to sit apart from Exit Sign:
# A major at 110, offbeat verse hats, a borrowed minor iv, and a flat-side bridge.
# Each chord below lasts one bar; every pitched part stays on that bar's chord tones.
# Chords intro: A | D | F#m | E
# Chords verse: A | Bm | D | E | A | C#m | F#m | E | A | D | Bm | E
# Chords pre: F#m | D | A | Bm | E | E
# Chords chorus: A | E | D | F#m | A | D | Dm | E
# Chords bridge: C | F | Am | Dm | Bb | G | E | E
# Chords outro: A | D | Dm | A
# Form 1-4: intro - Clean guitar alone, then bass, then a soft count
# Form 5-16: verse - Verse 1: clean answers in the gaps, held piano chords, offbeat hats
# Form 17-22: pre - Pre-chorus 1: the vocal climbs; a tom fill opens the chorus
# Form 23-30: chorus - Chorus 1: the hook, still held back, no guitar wall
# Form 31-42: verse - Verse 2: a new vocal line, rim then snare, ride cymbal
# Form 43-48: pre - Pre-chorus 2: the same climb, louder
# Form 49-56: chorus - Chorus 2: the wall arrives, open hats, a fill into the drop
# Form 57-64: bridge - Bridge: two bars of clean guitar and voice, then half-time in a new key
# Form 65-72: chorus - Final chorus A: full band, crashes, a fill into the last one
# Form 73-80: chorus - Final chorus B: the biggest pass; the minor iv is held longer
# Form 81-84: outro - Outro: the opening figure and the F natural, then home
# The verse snare drags 20 ticks; the last chorus tightens to 14.
# Plain style instrument names only, so a remix still falls back to each style's own patches.
# Reworked slower (72 BPM, from 110) with a Ben Folds-style piano on the chords; the piano uses
# inst=bank:grand-piano so it stays a piano in every remix. The power-chord chugs are gone: the
# piano drives the rhythm.
# The melody is a soft guitar (built from the harp), written an octave lower with its quick pickups merged, and the
# bass plays only roots.
# The melody is played lazily: every note sits 14-40 ticks (about 15-35 ms) behind the beat, the
# first in each bar the least, with small uneven velocities, from a fixed-seed generator.
title: Porch Light
composer: Grok, Claude & SZ
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
style: altrock
key: A major
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
about: A light left on at a slow, emo pace: clean guitar and a piano carry the verses, a borrowed minor chord turns the hook, and the band waits until the last chorus to get loud.

